# SHA-256 of the FROZEN isochrone set the primary analysis was computed against.
#
# Pinned because the wrong set is indistinguishable from the right one by name,
# path or file size. The local directory run_panel.sh used to point at
# (/Users/tylermuffly/isochrones/artifacts/isochrones) carries 3,909 coord_ids;
# the frozen set carries 4,050. The 141 missing origins included five that five
# subspecialties needed, and with unmatched_supply_policy = "drop" their supply
# silently vanished -- 12 of 14 cells, 68 origins, and a C5 ordering that
# depended on a margin the loss manufactured.
#
# Nine isochrone directories exist across this Mac and the Samsung drive. NONE
# of them matches these hashes. The frozen set was recovered from
#   s3://tyler-valhalla-tiles/seam_run/inputs/isochrones/
# which is where the EC2 launcher stages it. Fetch with:
#   aws s3 sync s3://tyler-valhalla-tiles/seam_run/inputs/isochrones/ "$E2SFCA_ISO_DIR"
#
# Hashes are from the frozen run's own input manifest
# (artifacts/2sfca_recovered/e2sfca_inputs_SHA256SUMS.txt), not recomputed from
# a copy that happened to be lying around.
